# S5-07 marker ordering experiment with a pre-marker guest delay

Date: 2026-11-16

## Purpose and scope

Test whether moving the existing checked 1 ms `nanosleep` in Stage 4 `/init`
before its nonce write prevents Linux's deferred `Run /init as init process`
printk from being concatenated with `OD_NONCE=...`. This was an isolated
diagnostic: the tracked Stage 4 fixture, runner, marker validator, comparator,
and acceptance rules were not modified.

An initial 500,000,000-retirement run stopped at virtual time 0.5 s, before
`/init`; UART was empty, so it provides no evidence about marker ordering. The
useful experiment below ran an automatic unique-nonce N=2 series to 2.6 billion
retirements per run.

## Candidate initramfs

The candidate `/init` source was built in a temporary directory by moving the
fixture's existing checked 1 ms `nanosleep` block before the marker-output
block. The `getpid` check remains after marker output. The original fixture was
not edited.

- Tracked `init.S` SHA-256: `6c7bb5bbaa84e9d0a1e27351c12c9f6a8d0efb6006b2eef982582ded9620f728`.
- Candidate source SHA-256: `3ee342e45095f1c4dc0ed1e47f7451609607063aedb34b1e4689b6c8ab271151`.
- Candidate `/init` ELF SHA-256: `fad513259cd88ba9d50c51aeccd1a8d50a1d09ab8a98f80cec9d11b36c00daff`.
- Candidate initramfs SHA-256: `65acac38cd4c791154f33179fe2c9f2103dd7fdec51aacfd969ab4d9eb0aedb7`.
- Build tools: Apple clang 21.0.0 and LLD 23.1.1.

The candidate input and build manifest are retained under the ignored
`work/stage5/s5-07-marker-delay-before-nonce/` directory.

## Series command and inputs

The exact command was:

```sh
target/release/od-runner linux-direct \
  --test-runs 2 \
  --series-id stage5-s5-07-marker-delay-before-nonce-n2-20261116-a \
  --scenario-id stage4-init-nonce \
  --expected-stop-kind budget_exhausted \
  --out work/stage5/stage5-s5-07-marker-delay-before-nonce-n2-20261116-a/series.json \
  --vmlinuz /Users/senya/projects/open_desktop/work/stage4/linux-7.0.0-38.38/vmlinuz-7.0.0-38-generic \
  --initramfs work/stage5/s5-07-marker-delay-before-nonce/initramfs.cpio \
  --acpi-blob tests/fixtures/guest/stage4/acpi_blob/stage4_acpi_blob.bin \
  --expected-vmlinuz-sha256 9f55ef7253055a9cf68f8a04323c93dead2fca617386d842fbde9ca7b178b27e \
  --expected-initramfs-sha256 65acac38cd4c791154f33179fe2c9f2103dd7fdec51aacfd969ab4d9eb0aedb7 \
  --expected-acpi-manifest-hash 2bd690ae0817705b1b128675f9628dd7212fee74ab97c88da3599a1ae8e398f2 \
  --ram-mib 128 --run --budget 2600000000 --set-cpl0 \
  --cpuid-profile stage4a --user-mode --execution-observations
```

`--linux-norandmaps` was not used. The command exited 1 because the strict
within-series comparator found unexplained differences; both guest scenarios
themselves passed.

